# Intent: Bench only (CONFIG_MAIPAI_SERIAL_TOOLS). self.bench.barge_test {count, gap_ms, no_barge, silent} runs rounds of talking over the unit with no person: the unit speaks a canned reply, then two wake hits reach the wake decision at the given gap as the detector's own event (Application::BenchInjectWakeHit), and each round prints "MaipaiBarge round=N interrupted=0|1 ms=N". self.bench.say_test and the rounds can run silent: the speaker volume is 0 and the echo reference is injected digitally into the loopback channel of the microphone path, so the echo canceller and the interruption path run with no sound (the silence_ms line then measures how fast the unit drops the reply, not the speaker). self.bench.say_test also takes silent.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/xiaozhi-esp32/main/application.h (nested tree, MIT); firmware/main/hal (ours)
# Check after a flash: on an aec bench image, self.bench.barge_test {count 3, gap_ms 600} prints three MaipaiBarge round lines with interrupted=1 and no sound with silent=1; with no_barge=1 they read interrupted=0.
# Kconfig: none new

